    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner, returning **409 Conflict**. This follows the existing pattern used for duplicate telephone/household checks.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending lower-cased email, mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` step in `addOwner`, invoked right after `normalizeEmail(...)` (so the incoming value is already trimmed/lower-cased). It compares the new email against each existing owner's stored email lower-cased, and throws the new exception on a match. Owners without an email and requests with no email are skipped.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` returning 409 Conflict with an `errors` array naming `email`, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (create owner with an email, then a second owner reusing it \u2192 expects 409) passes.",
